    <string name="privacy_policy">Privacy &amp; Data Security</string>
    <string name="privacy_policy_effective_date">Policy Updated: November 2026</string>
    <string name="privacy_policy_intro">ChatOn is built on a core philosophy: zero cloud dependence and total user privacy. Your conversations, documents, system instructions, and generated tokens remain strictly on your physical Android hardware. No analytics, tracking, or cloud telemetries are embedded.</string>
    <string name="privacy_policy_s1_title">1. Absolute Data Sovereignty</string>
    <string name="privacy_policy_s1_body">I, Om Thakur, engineer of ChatOn, believe personal computing should be truly personal. ChatOn requires no user registration, enforces no cloud account requirements, and runs no analytics trackers. Your data is yours alone.</string>
    <string name="privacy_policy_s2_title">2. Edge Computing Architecture</string>
    <string name="privacy_policy_s2_body">All natural language generation and vector embedding computations are performed natively by your device\'s chipset via llama.cpp. Your queries are never uploaded to any remote server or third-party AI provider for processing.</string>
    <string name="privacy_policy_s3_title">3. Minimal Network Access</string>
    <string name="privacy_policy_s3_body">Network permission is used exclusively for downloading the model files you explicitly request from Hugging Face repositories, or for external tool lookups if you opt-in. The core application functions 100% offline.</string>
    <string name="privacy_policy_s4_title">4. Sandboxed Tool Execution</string>
    <string name="privacy_policy_s4_body">Optional tools (Web search and Fetch page) communicate directly with target public endpoints only when toggled on by you. The integrated JavaScript engine executes within an isolated on-device sandbox without network access.</string>
    <string name="privacy_policy_s5_title">5. Ongoing Maintenance</string>
    <string name="privacy_policy_s5_body">Any technical enhancements or architecture updates will be posted to omthakur.in. Users are invited to explore the project code and technical thesis.</string>
    <string name="privacy_policy_s6_title">6. Agreement</string>
    <string name="privacy_policy_s6_body">By utilizing ChatOn, you benefit from local, decentralized on-device AI. For inquiries or collaboration, contact Om Thakur at omthakur2366@gmail.com.</string>
    <string name="privacy_policy_s7_title">7. Developer Inquiries</string>
    <string name="privacy_policy_s7_body">Have ideas, bug reports, or feedback for ChatOn? Reach out directly via email or visit omthakur.in.</string>
    <string name="privacy_policy_contact_email" translatable="false">omthakur2366@gmail.com</string>
    <string name="send_feedback">Email Om Thakur</string>
    <string name="faq">Help &amp; Knowledge Base</string>
    <string name="faq_subtitle">Architectural concepts and user guide</string>

    <!-- FAQ -->
    <string name="faq_q1">What makes ChatOn different from other AI apps?</string>
    <string name="faq_a1">ChatOn executes generative AI models directly on your smartphone\'s processor using native C++ kernels (llama.cpp). Unlike apps that stream requests to commercial cloud servers, ChatOn gives you complete offline availability, absolute data security, and zero subscription costs.</string>
    <string name="faq_q2">Which AI models are compatible with ChatOn?</string>
    <string name="faq_a2">ChatOn supports any modern architecture quantized in GGUF format (Q4_K_M, Q3_K_M, etc.), including DeepSeek R1 Distill, Qwen 3.5, Google Gemma 3 &amp; 4, Meta Llama 3.2, and Microsoft Phi-4 Mini.</string>
    <string name="faq_q3">What storage capacity is required?</string>
    <string name="faq_a3">Model files typically span from 500 MB (compact models like Qwen 0.6B) to 4–5 GB (high-capacity models like DeepSeek 7B). We recommend having at least 4 to 8 GB of free internal storage.</string>
    <string name="faq_q4">Does ChatOn require an internet connection?</string>
    <string name="faq_a4">Internet is only needed during initial model weight downloads and optional web search tools. Once a model is saved to your phone, ChatOn runs seamlessly in airplane mode without internet access.</string>
    <string name="faq_q5">How is my personal data protected?</string>
    <string name="faq_a5">ChatOn has no tracking servers, telemetry trackers, or database sync. Every token of chat history is stored in an encrypted local SQLite database on your device and never egresses outside.</string>
    <string name="faq_q6">How does device hardware affect token speed?</string>
    <string name="faq_a6">Generation speed depends on your mobile processor (ARM Cortex cores, memory bandwidth, and GPU/NPU support). Modern chipsets generate responses in seconds using ARM NEON vector instructions.</string>
    <string name="faq_q7">What hardware configuration is recommended?</string>
    <string name="faq_a7">For optimal experience, a device with 6 GB RAM or higher is recommended for 1B–3B models, and 8 GB to 12 GB RAM for 7B+ parameter reasoning models.</string>
    <string name="faq_q8">Can I import my own custom GGUF models?</string>
    <string name="faq_a8">Yes! Save any GGUF file into the ChatOn storage directory configured in Settings \u2192 Models. ChatOn dynamically inspects the file\'s metadata and makes it available in the chat picker immediately.</string>
    <string name="faq_q9">How can I select a different storage folder?</string>
    <string name="faq_a9">Navigate to Settings \u2192 Models and tap \u201CChange Folder\u201D to pick an internal folder or high-speed SD card via Android Storage Access Framework.</string>
    <string name="faq_q10">How do I remove unused models to free space?</string>
    <string name="faq_a10">Go to Settings \u2192 Models, view your \u201CDownloaded\u201D models list, and tap the delete icon next to the model you wish to purge.</string>
    <string name="faq_q11">What are System Prompts in ChatOn?</string>
    <string name="faq_a11">System prompts are behavioral instructions that guide the AI\'s persona, response tone, or formatting rules. You can save multiple custom prompts and apply them on-the-fly to any conversation.</string>
    <string name="faq_q12">What tool capabilities can models access?</string>
    <string name="faq_a12">Capable models can invoke tool calls mid-stream: Sandboxed JavaScript for math and algorithms, Web Search for real-time headlines, and Web Fetch for webpage summarization.</string>
    <string name="faq_q13">Are tool calls private?</string>
    <string name="faq_a13">JavaScript execution is 100% offline and sandboxed. When search is triggered, queries are dispatched directly to public search engines without passing through intermediary servers.</string>
    <string name="faq_q14">Does ChatOn generate in the background?</string>
    <string name="faq_a14">Yes. ChatOn runs the inference engine in a dedicated foreground service so Android OS does not evict long generations. A status notification updates live with token counts and progress.</string>
    <string name="faq_q15">Is voice recognition processed on-device?</string>
    <string name="faq_a15">Yes! Tapping the microphone leverages an offline speech-to-text neural network. Voice audio is never sent over any network and is transcribed purely in device RAM.</string>

